  "tagline": "Apache-licensed, foundation-governed fork of Elasticsearch for search, vectors and observability.",
  "description": "OpenSearch began in 2021 as AWS's Apache-2.0 fork of Elasticsearch 7.10 and has been governed by the Linux Foundation's OpenSearch Software Foundation since 2024. The 3.x line moved to Lucene 10 and invested heavily in vector workloads: Faiss and Lucene k-NN engines, disk-optimized and GPU-accelerated index builds, neural and hybrid search pipelines, plus PPL and SQL for log analytics. It is the natural pick if you want Elasticsearch-style search with a permissive license and no single-vendor control, or if you already run Amazon OpenSearch Service. API compatibility with modern Elasticsearch has drifted, so treat them as cousins rather than drop-in twins.",
